    feed_child() makes a pane re-emit "commit" (asynchronously on some VTE
    builds), which defeated every commit-based guard and let one keystroke
    avalanche across every pane. key-press-event fires only for real keyboard
    input and is never emitted by feed_child(), so replaying keys to the other
    panes cannot loop. Verified: one keystroke yields exactly one character
    per pane with no cascade.

 -- Sysible <sysiblesoftware@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:27:48 +0000

systerm (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Broadcast: suppress the fed panes' echo at its source. feed_child()
    makes a pane synchronously re-emit "commit"; we now block each target's
    commit handler across the write so that echo can't re-enter and fan out.
    This no longer depends on focus tracking or a timing-sensitive flag.

 -- Sysible <sysiblesoftware@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:11:55 +0000

systerm (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix broadcast amplification: one keystroke could fan out repeatedly and
    fill every pane with copies of each character. Only the focused pane's
    input fans out; the fed panes' echoes are ignored.

 -- Sysible <sysiblesoftware@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 18:54:49 +0000

